n01 Jun 2025 to 01 Jun 2035\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nFeedstocks\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nNULIFE GreenTech utilizes patented Hydrothermal Liquefaction (HTL) technology to convert waste biomass into carbon dense bio-oil. The Ontario Avenue project is in Saskatoon, SK, Canada. The Project utilizes wet and dry waste biomass from local food processing facilities. The bio-oil is transported to a third-party injection site for sequestration into a Canadian underground salt cavern. This project is the first commercial deployment of NULIFE’s modular and rapidly deployable HTL technology. The Ontario Avenue site will act as a showcase facility to validate unmatched biomass feedstock flexibility and versatile output capabilities for a range of high-value co-products.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\nNormec Verifavia\\n->\\nProject code\\nGHYZ\\nApproval date\\n30 Sep 2025\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBio-oil Geological Storage v1.2\\nBaseline protocol version\\nBio-oil Geological Storage v1.1\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nOntario Avenue Bio-Oil Sequestration\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n30 Sep 2025\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 45.83 tCO₂e removed from Ontario Avenue Bio-Oil Sequestration on 22 Jul 2026\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n45.835 t\\nSequestrations\\n47.591 t\\n-\\nActivities\\n1.709 tCO₂e\\n+\\nCounterfactuals\\n1 kgCO₂e\\n-\\nUncertainty Discount\\n45 kg\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nFeedstocks\\n\\nFeedstocks are the validated input materials that have been used for this project.\\n\\nName\\tCategory\\tValidated\\nBran Waste\\tBiomass\\t02 Apr 2026\\nEffluent Sludge\\tBiomass\\t02 Apr 2026\\nOat Hulls\\tBiomass\\t02 Apr 2026\\nShowing 3 of 3\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n26 Aug 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n26 Aug 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n27 Jul 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n27 Jul 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n18 Jun 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 5 of 18\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n1,404.08\\nRetired\\n329.619\\nBuffer pool\\n14.052\\nCrediting period\\n01 Jun 2025 to 01 Jun 2035\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nRefunds\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n26 Aug 2026\\t150.45\\t1.507\\t148.943\\n27 Jul 2026\\t205.43\\t2.056\\t203.374\\n18 Jun 2026\\t125.04\\t2.502\\t122.538\\n19 May 2026\\t296.87\\t5.94\\t290.93\\n20 Mar 2026\\t271.86\\t5.439\\t266.421\\n29 Dec 2025\\t58.54\\t1.171\\t57.369\\n26 Nov 2025\\t240.19\\t4.805\\t235.385\\n30 Sep 2025\\t55.7\\t1.114\\t54.586\\nShowing 8 of 8\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 1% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to NULIFE GreenTech's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 14.052 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 14.052 certificates.\\n\\nNULIFE GreenTech has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"